{{!-- Lifetime upgrade row — the one place an EXISTING member can buy
     Lifetime. Everywhere else, being a member is a dead end: /membership/
     swaps the pricing cards (Lifetime included) for "You're already a
     member", and /manage/ offers only Portal billing. A member who wanted
     to go permanent had to be told, by hand, to cancel first and then buy,
     which is a step nobody should have to know and several people would
     get half-done.

     Hidden until assets/js/page/lifetime-upgrade.js clears the flag, so
     an existing lifetime member never sees a flash of an offer they
     already took. Hidden-by-default costs nothing when JS is off: the
     button POSTs to mo-membership, so it needs JS to work at all.

     The button is the same [data-lifetime-checkout] contract that
     partials/membership-pricing.hbs uses, handled by
     assets/js/lifetime-checkout.js. Those two are mutually exclusive
     branches of partials/membership-body.hbs, so the single global
     [data-lifetime-error] lookup in that script never has two targets. --}}
<div class="lifetime-upgrade"
     data-lifetime-upgrade
     data-member-status="{{@member.status}}"
     data-member-labels="{{#foreach @member.labels}}{{name}} {{/foreach}}"
     hidden>
  {{!-- .lifetime-upgrade-copy carries no CSS of its own. It exists only
       to group the text as one grid item against the action column. --}}
  <div class="lifetime-upgrade-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Lifetime</p>
    <h2 class="lifetime-upgrade-title"><em>Join permanently.</em></h2>
    {{!-- The cancel-and-refund sentence is conditional in its wording
         because it is conditional in fact. The worker only supersedes a
         subscription that costs more than $0 (a Ghost comp is a $0
         "Complimentary" subscription), so comped, gift, group, and
         student members have nothing to cancel and get no refund.
         Promising them one unconditionally would be a lie told at the
         moment they hand over $995. --}}
    <p class="lifetime-upgrade-body">
      $995, once. It includes everything in the Membership, plus a copy of Jake Meador's <em>In Search Of The Common Good</em>. If you are paying monthly or annually, we cancel that for you and refund the part of the term you have not used.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="lifetime-upgrade-action">
    <button
      type="button"
      class="btn btn-pill btn-dark"
      data-hm-goal="upgrade-lifetime"
      data-lifetime-checkout
      data-member-email="{{#if @member}}{{@member.email}}{{/if}}"
      data-member-name="{{#if @member}}{{@member.name}}{{/if}}"
    >
      <span class="btn-label">Upgrade to Lifetime</span>
      <span class="btn-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </button>
    <p class="btn-tagline">One-time. No renewal.</p>
    <p class="btn-error" data-lifetime-error role="alert"></p>
  </div>
</div>
<script src="{{asset "js/page/lifetime-upgrade.js"}}"></script>
